    "<a id=\"section2\"></a>\n",
    "# Section 2 : Why Deep Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Classical ML (Weeks 3-4) works well on **structured, tabular data** — rows and columns with clearly\n",
    "defined features. Deep learning shines where classical methods struggle: **images, text, audio**, and\n",
    "other high-dimensional, unstructured data with complex patterns.\n",
    "\n",
    "The key difference: a neural network learns its own useful features directly from raw data, instead of\n",
    "relying on features engineered by hand (like the `FamilySize` or `Deck` features built manually in Week\n",
    "4). This is exactly why neural networks power modern computer vision and NLP — the topics of Weeks 7-8,\n",
    "and directly relevant to this project's sentiment analysis text data.\n"
   ]
  },
