    "<a id=\"section4\"></a>\n",
    "# Section 4 : Layers and Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "Neurons are organized into **layers**, and data flows through them in order:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Layer | Role |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Input layer** | Receives the raw features — one node per feature (e.g. one node per word/token feature for text) |\n",
    "| **Hidden layer(s)** | Learn intermediate representations; more layers or wider layers = more capacity to learn complex patterns |\n",
    "| **Output layer** | Produces the final prediction — its shape depends on the task (e.g. 3 output nodes for positive/neutral/negative sentiment) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**\"Deep\" learning** simply means a network with **multiple hidden layers**. Each layer transforms its\n",
    "input and passes the result forward to the next layer, and stacking layers lets the network build\n",
    "increasingly abstract patterns — early layers might respond to simple patterns, while deeper layers\n",
    "combine those into more complex, task-specific representations.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b297b87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A Small Visual\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Shallow Neural Network:** A basic machine learning model with only **one hidden layer** between the input and output. It handles simple patterns and small datasets.\n",
    "* **Deep Neural Network:** A complex machine learning model with **two or more hidden layers** (often dozens or hundreds). It can learn intricate, high-level patterns from massive amounts of data like images or voice.\n",
    "\n",
