   "source": [
    "<a id=\"section5\"></a>\n",
    "# Section 5 : Weights and Biases Are What's Learned\n",
    "\n",
    "The **weights** and **biases** are the network's parameters — the numbers that actually get adjusted\n",
    "during training. A freshly created network starts with random weights and makes essentially random\n",
    "predictions; training is the process of nudging these weights, little by little, until the predictions\n",
    "become accurate.\n",
    "\n",
    "*How* that nudging works — the actual training process — is what Days 2-3 this week are about.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **The core idea to hold onto:** the neuron is not new math — it is the Week 2 dot product, plus a bias,\n",
    "> plus an activation function. A neural network is that same simple operation, stacked and repeated many\n",
    "> times over. Keeping this in mind is what demystifies deep learning.\n"
   ]
  },
